  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`notes/spikes/003-acs-spike.md` documents a proven (or documented-schema-simulated + clearly labelled) server-side round-trip: identity → `chat`-scoped server-minted token → thread w/ 30-day retention → AddParticipants → SendMessage → Event Grid `ChatMessageReceivedInThread` capture with the validation handshake.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A **send→persist latency** number is reported, with a recommended poll cadence relative to it (~5s target).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">**Echo-dedup** is confirmed: the ACS message id is stable + present on both the send response and the inbound event, and de-duping on it makes the own-echo a no-op.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A **`dotnet publish` compressed size delta** for `Azure.Communication.Chat` 1.4.0 + `Azure.Communication.Identity` 1.3.1 vs ~45.30 MB is reported with a go/no-go vs the 60 MB ceiling.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A "consumed by 010/011/012/030/031" section maps each finding to the production task it de-risks.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No ACS SDK reference leaked into `Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj`; no production `Services/Acs/` code was added; spike code is quarantined under `notes/spikes/`.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Gates ALL ACS work: 010 (identity/token), 011 (thread/membership), 012 (provisioning), 020 (channel sender/archiver over ACS), 030 (Event Grid ingress). Land it before W1 opens.

    The echo-dedup finding is load-bearing for the entire outbound/inbound coexistence (design §4). If the ACS message id proves NOT to be a stable dedupe key, that is a design-level finding — escalate before W3 (031) is built on it.

    Publish-size: design §8.9 predicts negligible (thin over `Azure.Core`, already present). If the measured delta contradicts that (≥+5 MB), flag it — it changes the root §10 posture for every ACS BFF task.

    If the ACS researcher memory file is absent (it is referenced by design/plan but may not be present in this worktree), run the `researcher` subagent to establish the findings and record that the memory file needed (re)creation.
  </notes>

